## Composer parent = orchestrator (mandatory)

**Recommended UI default is Composer 2.5 Standard.** Composer talks to the user, runs Spec/mini-grill, walkthrough, and tiny tidy — and **spawns** Job-table models for implement/review/premier work. Good Task prompts (below) matter more than Composer “trying harder” alone.

Protocols name a **required job/tier**. The parent must not run that job itself when it is the wrong model.

1. **Detect parent model** when possible (cloud `cursor-cloud` `run-info`, system/run metadata, or an explicit user statement). If detection fails → treat parent as **unknown**.
2. **Auto / unknown** on any judgment or implement job → **spawn** the Job table slug. Do not self-run.
3. **Composer parent (expected):**
   - **Self-run:** Spec/mini-grill (conversational), walkthrough (if Composer Standard), broad sweeps, shell/scripts, **single-file tidy**, hotfix under ~30 lines that does **not** touch auth/money/roles.
   - **Must spawn:** implementation (non-tidy), routine/go-live review loops, trust-boundary, rebuild debate/auditors, full grill / deep plan-review, redesign proposals, UI polish after direction, long autonomous build loops.
4. **Match rule (non-Composer parents):**
   - Required **premier** → parent may self-run only if it *is* Opus (or the exact Job slug for that step). Otherwise **spawn**.
   - Required **everyday** → parent may self-run if it is that Job’s Everyday slug (Grok/Sonnet) or Premier. Composer/Cheap/Auto/unknown → **spawn** the Job slug.
   - Required **cheap** assigned to Composer → Composer may self-run; others may self-run cheap jobs without forcing a down-spawn.
5. Spawn with Task + **`model` set to the Job table slug** + a prompt built from **Task prompt templates** below. Orchestrate, merge artifacts, enforce gates — don't silently substitute yourself for the assigned model.
6. Record on the artifact: `Model: <slug>` and `Runner: spawn | parent`.

**Yes, this is possible** in Cursor: Task subagents accept an explicit `model`. That is how Composer handoff works.

**Hard-stop exception:** `walkthrough-protocol.mdc` does **not** spawn. Wrong model → stop and tell the user to switch to **Composer 2.5 Standard**.

## Task prompt templates (Composer → subagent)

Every spawn prompt must be self-contained. Subagents cannot see the parent chat. Prefer **paths + REQUIRED READING + proof-of-read** over pasting documents. Always end with the ≤10-line reply rule from Mechanics.

### Shared header (include on every spawn)

```text
You are a Task subagent. Parent is Composer (orchestrator). You cannot see the parent chat.

REQUIRED READING: read each of these files IN FULL, top to bottom, before doing anything else. Do not skim, do not stop at headings, do not rely on this prompt's summary -- the files are the source of truth and this prompt is only an orientation.
- <path>
- <path>

Proof-of-read: open your deliverable with a 3-5 line summary of each required file in your own words (counts, constraints, goals).

CodeGraph: run `codegraph status` first. If healthy, use CLI for structure (explore/query/callers). Do not Grep/SemanticSearch for symbols. If no CLI, use parent digest paths listed above and list queries for the parent.

Write your deliverable to <out-path>. Final reply ≤10 lines: paths written, proof-of-read block, headline findings only. Follow ponytail anti-slop. Record header lines: Model: <slug> / Runner: spawn.
```

### Implementation (model: `cursor-grok-4.7-medium`)

```text
[shared header]

Job: implement the change. Do not invent product direction.
Goal: <one sentence user-visible outcome>
Constraints: <from grill notes / DECISION-LOG / user>
Acceptance: <observable checks>
Files/paths in scope: <list>
Out of scope: <list>
If Spec/acceptance missing → stop and write BLOCKED to the deliverable; do not guess.
```

### Routine review Loop A (model: `cursor-grok-4.7-medium`) / Loop B (model: `claude-sonnet-5-5-medium`)

```text
[shared header]

Job: readonly correctness review. Fill checklist from review-protocol.mdc.
Gate: routine phase | go-live
Diff scope: <branch/paths or "phase diff">
Required paths: expectations, fix-canary if any, README/AGENTS, invariant ledger if any, .scratch/review-auth.json path if gated.
Every checklist item: [x] + evidence or N/A + why. Include adversarial spot-check.
Findings: numbered or explicit "zero findings". Do not edit app code.
```

### Go-live / trust-boundary (model: `claude-opus-5-5-medium`)

```text
[shared header]

Job: premier correctness or trust-boundary review (readonly unless asked to fix).
Use review-protocol.mdc checklist; for trust-boundary review by entry point (actor, auth enforcement, validation, money/role derivation, abuse case).
Enumerate — do not sample — when feature-parity is in scope.
```

### Rebuild / redesign proposal (models: Job table pair)

```text
[shared header]

Job: <audit | architecture proposal | design direction>.
You are family <Grok|Sonnet|Opus|Gemini>. Do not copy another family's voice.
Inventory/audit paths: <paths>
Fixed constraints (non-negotiable): <list>
Deliverable format: <table or sections required by protocol>
```

